.idea/
.claude/
.superpowers/

node_modules/
out/
dist-installer/
packages/*/dist/
# `npm install` in an examples folder links the SDK package there; the lock it writes names this checkout only.
examples/*/package-lock.json

# Build inputs that are fetched, not authored: the Host's runtime payload (a pinned node.exe and the
# files copied around it — scripts/host-runtime.mjs) and the download cache behind it. Pinned by
# version and SHA-256 in that script, so the bytes are reproducible without committing 90 MB.
resources/host-runtime/
build/.cache/

# docs/ is handled as a whitelist. Everything else there is design and planning notes that stay
# local — written this way round so a new note defaults to "not published".
docs/*
!docs/releasing.md
!docs/slack-bot-setup.md
!docs/jobs.md
!docs/how-it-works.md
!docs/usage-guide.md
# Published deliberately: `astera` is a public interface, and the README links to this reference.
!docs/cli.md
# Published deliberately: `astera mcp serve` is a public interface, and the README links to it.
!docs/mcp.md
# Published deliberately: @astera-app/client is a public interface, and cli.md, mcp.md and the package README link to it.
!docs/sdk.md
# Published deliberately: the plugin author's guide, which cli.md, sdk.md, the README and the plugin SDK's README link to.
!docs/plugins.md
# Published deliberately: `--runtime` and MCP's `runtimeId` are public interfaces, and cli.md and mcp.md link to it.
!docs/remote-runtime.md
# Published deliberately: a design brief that outlives the branch it was written on, because the work
# it describes is picked up in another session and often another worktree, where an ignored file does
# not exist. It says on its face that nothing in it is decided yet.
!docs/agent-workspace-isolation.md
# Published deliberately: where the freeze and slowness work stopped, so the next session (possibly on
# another machine, where the ignored ledgers do not exist) can pick it up.
!docs/2026-09-28-next-session-handoff.md
# Published deliberately: the SignPath Foundation requires the code signing policy to be reachable at
# a public URL, and the README links to it.
!docs/code-signing.md
# Published deliberately: the filled Mac check (scripts/mac-check) of 2026-10-29, so the next Mac run
# can be set beside it, on whatever machine it is done.
!docs/2026-10-29-mac-check-results.md
# Not a note but an input: scripts/build-release-notes.cjs reads docs/release-notes/<tag>.md out of
# the checkout the publish job makes at the tag, so a write-up that is not committed does not exist.
!docs/release-notes/

# The source brand sheet (a 1254x1254 mockup). Icons are cropped from it and only the outputs are
# committed — see scripts/gen-icon.ps1.
astera.png
